94139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532777 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532780 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1077 "II" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1078 #edb/ref 17592186532780 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532775 1079 #uuid "6b93784d-4281-5760-8eef-4865819e8b08" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1068 #edb/ref 17592186532774 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1068 #edb/ref 17592186532775 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1068 #edb/ref 17592186532778 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1068 #edb/ref 17592186532779 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1071 "![](images/ac/ac756d7cbd687a23a5b2c1ffcb368298f4676178e8bebccbadd4e837fe66a3d7.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1072 #uuid "7f1277c2-1732-59aa-9938-5b092ddfb7eb" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532776 1074 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that $F$ represents the velocity field of flowing water. Place a paddlewheel at $P$ with its axis in the $z$-direction. If it rotates, the field has nonzero curl; if it does not, the field has zero curl.\n\nThe arrows turn a paddlewheel counterclockwise. Thus $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ throughout space, so $F$ is not irrotational. Curl measures local rotation, even when the arrows also spread outward. Wrap the fingers of your right hand in the counterclockwise direction: your thumb points out of the screen, in the positive $z$-direction.\n\nWith that in mind, check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false.\n- Statement II is true.\n- Statement III is false.\n- Statement IV is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532777 1080 "false" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532777 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532777 1083 #uuid "83d545a1-3cb7-50ad-afd2-99914e5c776e" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532771 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532781 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1077 "I" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1078 #edb/ref 17592186532781 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532778 1079 #uuid "902b4a07-6d8b-5503-adc1-c2e50d71cada" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532770 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532772 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1077 "III" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1078 #edb/ref 17592186532772 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532779 1079 #uuid "d88cb888-c4d7-5ba8-baab-76faa9062e42" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532780 1080 "true" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532780 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532780 1083 #uuid "e99e88eb-25ca-5d9e-a643-ad008b0e980a" 13194139535845 17592186045443 true] [17592186532781 1080 "false" 13194139535845 1759218604544